WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:05.460
From Star Search to The Ellen DeGeneres&nbsp;
Show, Stephen "tWitch" Boss was a rare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.000
talent and outgoing presence on&nbsp;
television for nearly two decades.
 &nbsp;

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.980
Despite lots of stories about how tWitch&nbsp;
got his name, claiming it was because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.920
never sat still as a kid, Boss himself told&nbsp;
AL.com in 2013 that he gave himself the name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.540
after a car he owned that "would accelerate&nbsp;
on its own sometimes." According to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.860
he would come up with a lot of his choreography&nbsp;
while he was on the road to different performances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.540
and teaching dance around the state of Alabama,&nbsp;
where he grew up. Boss told the outlet:

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:39.000
"I was about 20 years old ... when I first started&nbsp;
dancing, going places and teaching dance."
 &nbsp;

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.800
Before garnering a coveted spot on the&nbsp;
star-making show So You Think You Can Dance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.360
Stephen "tWitch" Boss competed in — and&nbsp;
nearly won — two other dance-related talent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:53.160
competitions. Early in his dance career, tWitch&nbsp;
competed on the ubiquitous celebrity-magnet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.800
talent show Star Search. Rebooted from the&nbsp;
original Ed McMahon juggernaut in 2003,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.800
Star Search came back on the air to CBS with&nbsp;
host Arsenio Hall. It only lasted a year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.760
but in that time tWitch not only made&nbsp;
it on, but he was also the runner-up.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.260
Also in 2003, tWitch competed on&nbsp;
MTV's The Wade Robson Project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:19.380
where dancers would battle against each other&nbsp;
for a grand prize of $100,000, making it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:24.600
the semifinals. Boss clearly remained a fan of&nbsp;
the legendary dancer and choreographer, as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.400
performed at least two solos to Robson's music&nbsp;
during his time on So You Think You Can Dance.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.400
In that same interview, Boss&nbsp;
revealed that if he hadn't made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.240
it onto So You Think You Can Dance,&nbsp;
he would've joined the Navy, saying,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.880
"[E]verything I'm experiencing&nbsp;
now is because of the show."
 &nbsp;

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:44.100
It's not easy to get on So You Think You Can&nbsp;
Dance. First, there are auditions in cities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.720
around the country for anyone and everyone&nbsp;
who thinks they can dance. A panel of judges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.820
generally made up of executive producer Nigel&nbsp;
Lythgoe and a selection of acclaimed industry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:58.260
professionals, oversee the process. They&nbsp;
either give the contestant a pass straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.920
on to the next round in Las Vegas,&nbsp;
or they ask performers to come back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.100
later that day for some structured&nbsp;
choreography for a second chance.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:10.080
Las Vegas Week is grueling, as everyday&nbsp;
dancers are charged with learning a routine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.540
from a star choreographer in a different genre&nbsp;
of dance, from hip-hop to jazz to ballroom to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.040
contemporary. Only those who pass that entire&nbsp;
week will be up for consideration to compete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:25.560
on the live shows. Boss auditioned in Season&nbsp;
3 but didn't make the cut. He was undeterred,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:30.060
however, and in Season 4 he came back&nbsp;
and not only made it to the Top 20 but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:33.660
was still standing in the finale,&nbsp;
finishing second to Joshua Allen.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.620
Since then, he returned to So You&nbsp;
Think You Can Dance multiple times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:43.200
performing as a special guest or all-star, and&nbsp;
was part of dozens of unforgettable routines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.360
one of which even caught the eye of a certain&nbsp;
Ellen DeGeneres, leading to a new opportunity.
&nbsp;

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:55.560
In 2010, Fox aired Season 7 of the popular dance&nbsp;
competition So You Think You Can Dance. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:00.840
seventh season was the first to feature All-Stars,&nbsp;
in which popular contestants from previous seasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.340
would pair with the new dancers competing&nbsp;
for the current title. It was here that Boss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:10.620
a contestant and runner-up from Season 4,&nbsp;
met Allison Holker, a standout talent from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.720
Season 2. Allison was instantly attracted&nbsp;
to Stephen, as she insisted on calling him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.280
and made the first move, as she told Jennifer&nbsp;
Hudson on the latter's daytime talk show.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.460
"You know, I was out there making&nbsp;
all these moves and it took him a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.820
second to see them but once he did, you&nbsp;
know, we locked it in. We locked it in."

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:31.620
Boss eventually "locked it down," though,&nbsp;
and the couple married in 2013. Since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.040
their fairytale marriage has been followed&nbsp;
by millions of fans on TikTok and Instagram,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.260
has produced two children, and even got them&nbsp;
a hosting gig on Disney's Fairy Tale Weddings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:44.100
showcasing mega Disney fans getting&nbsp;
married at one of the resort's many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.640
properties. Upon announcing her&nbsp;
husband's death, Holker promised:

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.860
"I will always save the last dance for you."

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.500
Before his revealing role in Magic Mike XXL&nbsp;
as a male exotic dancer in a ladies' club,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.720
Stephen "tWitch" Boss racked up several dance&nbsp;
credits in films over the years. It all started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.840
in 2006 when he had a small, uncredited role as&nbsp;
"flamboyant dancer" in Blades of Glory. Following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:11.760
that, tWitch appeared as one of Mama Maybelle's&nbsp;
dancers in the Adam Shankman musical reboot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:17.280
Hairspray. Rounding out his resumé with Stomp&nbsp;
the Yard 2: Homecoming and installments three,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:22.440
four, and five of the Step Up franchise, tWitch&nbsp;
built a steady career out of and about dance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:27.540
Even in his cameo role on the TV series&nbsp;
Bones, he appeared as a street performer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:31.800
dancing for the passersby and hoping&nbsp;
for a few bucks in his proffered hat.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:37.200
Stephen Boss was a man meant to dance, and&nbsp;
when he met Allison Holker they seemed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.560
speak in a language of dance all their&nbsp;
own. He proposed to her through dance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.760
They announced their first pregnancy together&nbsp;
through dance. They performed together on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.900
Dancing with the Stars when Allison worked&nbsp;
there as one of the pros. They celebrated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:53.220
Allison's ninth month of pregnancy with&nbsp;
their second baby via a motivating dance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:57.660
and they warmed the hearts of followers&nbsp;
with family and friend dances on TikTok.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.640
It's not often that a celebrity can reach so many&nbsp;
people and resonate so strongly with their best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:07.200
dreams and hopes for the world, but Stephen&nbsp;
"tWitch" Boss was one of those men. He will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.720
be missed in every community that treasured his&nbsp;
unique combination of dance, laughter, and warmth.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:18.300
If you or anyone you know is having suicidal&nbsp;
thoughts, please call the National Suicide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:25.920
Prevention Lifeline​ by dialing 988&nbsp;
or by calling 1-800-273-TALK (8255)​.

